<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 17 March, from 461 to 1958.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">461</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Traditional date of the death of Saint Patrick</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition Patrick, the Romano-British missionary to Ireland, died on 17 March, though the year is uncertain. His feast became Ireland's national day, celebrated by the Irish diaspora worldwide.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1776</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British troops evacuate Boston</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Washington fortified Dorchester Heights with cannon hauled from Fort Ticonderoga, General Howe's army sailed for Halifax. The siege of Boston ended in an American success.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1845</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen Perry patents the rubber band</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stephen Perry of the London firm Messrs Perry and Co patented bands made of vulcanised rubber for holding papers together. The humble invention became universal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1905</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Einstein completes his paper on light quanta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Einstein finished a paper proposing that light comes in discrete packets of energy, explaining the photoelectric effect. It helped found quantum theory and earned him the Nobel Prize.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1948</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brussels Treaty creates a Western European defence pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Britain, France, Belgium, the Netherlands and Luxembourg agreed to defend one another against attack. The pact paved the way for NATO in 1949 and later became the Western European Union.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1958</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US launches Vanguard 1 satellite</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The grapefruit-sized satellite, mocked by Khrushchev, showed that the Earth is slightly pear-shaped. Long silent, it is the oldest human-made object still in orbit.</p></li></ol>
